    test+docs: fourth assignment -- interpolation-mode dispatch, tutor-authored, and the evaluator that never compiled
    
    Case 4 of the campaign, completing the author spectrum: gemma authored case 2,
    qwen3 case 3, and this one is TUTOR-AUTHORED -- gemma's third authoring run hung
    for 22 minutes producing a 0-byte journal (recorded as a jichi finding: a hang
    BEFORE the first tool boundary is outside every envelope budget) and was ended
    with a graceful SIGINT.
    
    THE DISCOVERY THAT RE-SCOPED IT: the assignment was meant to be
    AnimationEvaluator.interpolate_value's dispatch, and writing its gate found the
    evaluator struct has NEVER COMPILED when actually used -- its std.HashMap field
    predates the current 4-argument API, and no test had ever constructed the type.
    gate-lint counts test blocks, not analyzable types; the first constructing test
    is what found the dark region. The assignment is therefore the pure
    keyframes.interpolateWithMode (panic stub, three gate tests, spec-specific
    verify), with the evaluator's own repair stated as a separate task; the spec's
    context section tells the story so the learner knows why the shape is what it
    is.
    
    Gate proven RED via jichi grade --expect-fail (3 of 4 filtered tests crash on
    the stub); the reference solution (switch on mode: nearest snaps, linear
    delegates, cubic honestly falls back) was proven 4/4 + whole-suite green and
    reverted -- it lives with the case study in the jichi repository.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

